Scenario 3 — Resilient CSV Import

I reviewed the existing importcontroller, processimportjob and import job code. I identified several improvements needed
to make the import safer and easier to monitor.

I added a test to check that an invalid row does not prevent valid rows from being improted as this was part of the AC.
Before changing the implementation, I asked an LLM to produce a plan.md based on the scenario requirments. Reviewing the
lan first gave me the opportunity to correct and refine the approach before implemention began.

After reviewing the initial plan produced, i identified areas that needed more detial, including how to handle duplicate imports,
retries, progress, updates, and invalid rows. I reviewed the revised plan and made some future adjustments before starting the
implemention.

Once the plan was implemented, I ran `make reset && make test` and confirmed the tests where still passing. I then review
the changed code and found additional issues so made further changes to address these issues, improve malformed-row reporting
and protect rejected CSV downloads from spreadsheet formula execution.

I also removed tthe shared default password. Imports now require each row to provide a valid password, rather than asigning
every account the same predictable value.

Further improvements as possible, but i judged them to be outside the scope of this scenario.